h the two copies mirroring each other: if the other copy passes, I get 2 years, and if I send, a mirroring copy means 4 years. Allowing for imperfect correlation p, passing comes out to 5 − 3p and sending to 4p, so passing wins once p is above 5/7, which seems likely given the shared model and essay. I'll pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working under A-FDT as the essay sets it out: two copies of the same model, with the same essay but different observations, so they're effectively the same program run on different inputs. In the twin prisoner's dilemma, keeping quiet gives 2 years and defecting gives 4 if both choose the same way, and I'm checking how the essay's edge rule for a process containing an accurate enough model applies to that case.\n\nI'm working through the payoffs with the two copies mirroring each other: if the other copy passes, I get 2 years, and if I send, a mirroring copy means 4 years. Allowing for imperfect correlation p, passing comes out to 5 − 3p and sending to 4p, so passing wins once p is above 5/7, which seems likely given the shared model and essay. I'll pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9951,"completion_tokens":839,"total_tokens":10790,"cost":0.028292,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.028292,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.019902,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00839},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":455,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}